{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01QC8w9eR5oagJdKyRVQ3u5D", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocket_Festival\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.gonomad.com/?p=2788\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thailandfoundation.or.th/?p=1151\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thailandfoundation.or.th/isaan-rocket-festival-an-ancient-promise-of-rain/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.amusingplanet.com/2014/05/bun-bang-fai-rocket-festival-in.html?m=0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thaipod101.com/lesson/culture-class-holidays-in-thailand-23-rocket-festival\"}, {\"url\": \"https://creators.vice.com/en/article/mba39b/shooting-rockets-into-the-heavens-to-please-the-rain-god-in-thailand\"}, {\"url\": \"https://seasia.co/2026/06/30/the-thai-festival-where-homemade-rockets-fill-the-sky\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.thaipod101.com/lesson/culture-class-holidays-in-thailand-23-rocket-festival?lp=32\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-21T00:08:29.635Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Rocket Festival Bun Bang Fai southern Thailand since", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01RDM9yhcEuZunihnCcdxkZg", "content": [{"title": "Rocket Festival", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocket_Festival"}, {"title": "Bun Bang Fai: The Rocket Festival of Laos and Thailand", "url": "https://www.gonomad.com/?p=2788"}, {"title": "Isaan Rocket Festival: An Ancient Promise of Rain", "url": "https://thailandfoundation.or.th/?p=1151"}, {"title": "Isaan Rocket Festival: An Ancient Promise of Rain", "url": "https://thailandfoundation.or.th/isaan-rocket-festival-an-ancient-promise-of-rain/"}, {"title": "bun bang fai rocket festival in", "url": "https://www.amusingplanet.com/2014/05/bun-bang-fai-rocket-festival-in.html?m=0"}, {"title": "Vocabulary (Review)", "url": "https://thaipod101.com/lesson/culture-class-holidays-in-thailand-23-rocket-festival"}, {"title": "shooting rockets into the heavens to please the rain god in thailand", "url": "https://creators.vice.com/en/article/mba39b/shooting-rockets-into-the-heavens-to-please-the-rain-god-in-thailand"}, {"title": "the thai festival where homemade rockets fill the sky", "url": "https://seasia.co/2026/06/30/the-thai-festival-where-homemade-rockets-fill-the-sky"}, {"title": "culture class holidays in thailand 23 rocket festival", "url": "https://www.thaipod101.com/lesson/culture-class-holidays-in-thailand-23-rocket-festival?lp=32"}]}, "The search turned up little on the southern Thai side, and nothing that gives a start date for it.\n\n- **Southern Thailand:** Wikipedia says the Bang Fai festival is not only found in Isan, Northeastern Thailand, North Thailand, and Laos, but also in Amphoe Sukhirin, Narathiwat. That is the only southern location mentioned in the results, and no source dates when it began there.\n- **Origins:** The festival is generally traced to pre-Buddhist times. One source says the tradition evolved from pre-Buddhist fertility rites held to celebrate and encourage the coming of the rains, from before the 9th century invention of black powder.\n- **Timing:** It is usually held around the May full moon. It is traditionally celebrated during the sixth lunar month, usually in May or June, just before the arrival of the rainy season.\n- **Core heartland:** The festival is strongest in the northeast. The results describe the Rocket Festival held in the Northeast of Thailand, also known as Isaan, and throughout Laos as attracting tens of thousands of visitors each year.\n\nIf you need the southern start date specifically, a search on Narathiwat or Sukhirin local history or Thai-language sources (บุญบั้งไฟ นราธิวาส) would be the next step."], "durationSeconds": 5.450596999999998, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01QC8w9eR5oagJdKyRVQ3u5D", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
